From 879cde46b3daf74a2600b90673125135f4f5584c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:34:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 096/112] graph + mmap + model : SiegeLadder P8c - a prompt's
 Engram rows read straight from the model files (LLAMA_ENGRAM_PP_DIRECT=1,
 off; _DIRECT_THREADS / _DIRECT_QD, 8 x 32): llama_read_scattered - many small
 scattered reads through unbuffered overlapped I/O, each 4 KB sector once, its
 pieces copied out - into a compact per-layer buffer (256 bytes of FP8 + 8 of
 scale per row, ~95 MB on a 7.5K turn against 2.9 GB of faulted pages),
 fill_layer takes the rows from there; the model records where each engram
 layer's tables lie (llama_model::engram_src). Bitwise the same logits
 (bench/engram_pp_check.py arm d), but slow while the engram files are mapped
 by the process, as they are today: Windows checks the cache coherency of
 every unbuffered read of a mapped file - diskspd on part 2 did 13K reads a
 second with a server running against 1.0M without - and a 3K prompt read 22 s
 instead of 12 (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.238). Kept off as the building block for
 unmapped (streamed) engram tables

